From: David Yoon <5332544+yoonda9@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:29:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] win: TAZ-only pipe tests for the CancelIoEx fallbacks

Four tests in test/test-pipe-connect-multiple.c, registered in
test-list.h, all under the legacy guard so they vanish from the neutral
tree:
- taz_pipe_read_exact_fill: a read that exactly fills the buffer is
  delivered whole, then EOF, and in the forced build no zero read.
- taz_pipe_close_read_pending: uv_close cancels a pending read while a
  duplicate handle keeps the pipe open, so closing cannot abort it.
- taz_pipe_read_stop_write_pending: uv_read_stop with a write pending
  does not cancel the write, and a later uv_close completes with a
  duplicate handle open.
- taz_pipe_shutdown_after_read_stop: a uv_shutdown after that
  uv_read_stop does not report EOF to the stopped reader (Windows only:
  elsewhere a pipe's uv_shutdown sends EOF at once).

Existing tests drive the other fallback paths in the forced build: a
failed I/O packet in tcp_close_reset_client* and
tcp_close_reset_accepted* (the reset completes the pending read with an
error), and a TCP close with only a read pending in
tcp_close_after_read_timeout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
